[cot:thought] Key figures for the
[cot:thought] update post are now locked in. The 2025 AGR targets $310???365B by 2035, yet flows remain at $26B and the gap is $284???339B. Annual flows fell $2B, or 7.1%, year-over-year.
[cot:thought] The Glasgow target of roughly $40B will likely be missed. Private capital potential sits near $50B but current flows are only $5B.
[cot:thought] Debt instruments now comprise 58% of flows, while concessional lending makes up 70%.
[cot:thought] The MDB drop is the primary driver of the shortfall. Inflation-adjusted needs by 2035 are estimated at $440???520B. The NCQG pool of $300B is also deemed insufficient.
